# Shell scripts here run inside Linux containers. A CRLF checkout gives them a
# carriage return on the shebang line, and the kernel then looks for an
# interpreter literally named "/usr/bin/env bash\r" and reports "bad interpreter:
# no such file or directory" -- an error that names a file which plainly exists,
# which is why it costs an afternoon rather than a minute.
#
# Git on Windows converts by default, so without this a clone, an edit and a
# commit is enough to break bootstrap.sh for everyone. Pin them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Compose bundle's env template is read by the same shell.
*.env.example text eol=lf
